    "note": "Reengrossed (03/08/2018). Not the final act; amendments made after the version read are not in the text read. Both quotes are the new exceptions, which are exceptions to the offences of carrying a concealed weapon. Section 3 trims background-check and ID-unit appropriations to implement the act (not quoted); not a separate subject."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-105(2)(g)): A PERSON WHO WAS AT LEAST TWENTY-ONE YEARS OF AGE AND LEGALLY POSSESSED A HANDGUN UNDER THE LAWS OF THIS STATE AND OF THE UNITED STATES AND THE WEAPON INVOLVED IN THE INCIDENT WAS A HANDGUN. THE AUTHORITY TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THIS SUBSECTION (2)(g) IS EQUAL IN ALL RESPECTS TO THE AUTHORITY GRANTED BY A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN AS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214.\nSection 2 (C.R.S. 18-12-105.5(3)(i)): THE PERSON IS AT LEAST TWENTY-ONE YEARS OF AGE AND MAY LEGALLY POSSESS A HANDGUN UNDER THE LAWS OF THIS STATE AND OF THE UNITED STATES AND THE WEAPON INVOLVED IN THE INCIDENT WAS A HANDGUN. THE AUTHORITY TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THIS SUBSECTION (3)(i) IS EQUAL IN ALL RESPECTS TO THE AUTHORITY GRANTED BY A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN AS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214."
}